## Summary

I injected `data-semtag-*` hints across all 8 screens of **ThreadHive**, a forum app (WebTestBench_0019): Home, Category, Thread detail, New Thread, Login, Register, Profile, and NotFound.

**Shared components hinted (so hints propagate to every call site):**
- `Header.tsx` — logo, search, new-thread/profile/logout or login/register nav
- `Sidebar.tsx` — sort filters (toggle), categories collection
- `CategoryBadge.tsx` — widened with explicit `data-semtag-*` pass-through props (root differs: `<Link>` vs `<span>`), since it's used both as navigation and as a decorative label depending on context
- `ThreadCard.tsx` — widened with a required `collectionId` prop so the same card can be safely reused across 3 different lists
- `ReplyCard.tsx` — ids hardcoded under `thread.replies.item.<id>` since it only ever renders in one context

**Id namespaces introduced:**
- `nav.*` (Header), `search.query`, `feed.filter.*` / `feed.sort` (shared sort control)
- `sidebar.categories(.item.<id>)` — collection
- `home.threads` / `category.threads` / `profile.threads` — three distinct collections, each folding `ThreadCard` items as `<collection>.item.<threadId>[.upvote|.upvotes|.category|.author|.replyCount|.viewCount]`
- `thread.*` — single-instance detail-page elements, with `data-semtag-state` keyed as `threads.<id>.title/content/upvotes/replyCount/viewCount` so the same value can be cross-referenced between a card and the detail page
- `thread.replies(.item.<id>...)` — reply collection, plus `thread.replies.heading` (the header's own live count) kept **distinct** from `thread.replyCount` (the thread's stored `replyCount` field) — these two numbers come from different data and can drift, which is exactly the kind of defect this benchmark checks for
- `newThread.*`, `login.*`, `register.*`, `profile.*` (incl. `profile.interests` as a slug-keyed collection), `notfound.home`

**Collections I could not simplify further:** the profile interests list uses a slugified tag string as its domain key (no separate id exists in the data model) — noted as the one place a "key" is derived rather than sourced directly.

**Deliberately left unhinted:** the Sidebar's hardcoded "Community Stats" block (1,045 threads / 4,823 replies / etc.) — static numbers with no backing state, purely decorative; and the large `CategoryBadge` on `CategoryPage` (`asLink={false}`) — redundant with the new `category.heading` observable I added on the `<h1>` right below it.

Validator: 70 hinted elements, 0 errors/warnings even with `--strict`. `tsc --noEmit`, `vite build`, and `eslint` all pass; the only lint findings are pre-existing `react-refresh` warnings and one `tailwind.config.ts` `require()` error in files I never touched.

